# A public generic function that calls itself with its type parameter
# nested ever deeper has no finite set of instances. Other modules would
# make its instances, so it is reported where it is declared.

use lib

sub main()
  print(lib.nest(1))

# error: 4:9: `nest[T]` leads to ever deeper instances of generic functions (through `nest[Wrap[T]]`); a generic function cannot call itself with its own type parameters nested deeper
